\title{Record types as theories}
\import{prelude}

\p{Records types compose multiple theories into into a single theory, whose models consist of a model of each of its individual pieces. A record type declaration consists of a list of \em{fields}, each of which is declared to be a model of another theory. For instance:}

\pre{%
\kw{theory} SantaList := \kw{sig}
  naughty : Set
  nice : Set
\kw{end}
}

\p{\code{SantaList} is a very simple theory, the models of which consist of a pair of a collection of naughty things and a collection of nice things.}

